/Title (Forward path. A packet from the instance in VPC A to a 10.20.x.x address matches the 10.20.0.0/16 route in ewb-rt-a-private, whose target is the peering connection. It crosses the peering link and arrives in VPC B, where the destination security group must allow the traffic.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 886 0 R
/Next 966 0 R
>>
endobj
966 0 obj
<<
/Title (Return path. The reply to a 10.10.x.x address matches the 10.10.0.0/16 route in ewb-rt-b-private, which also points at the peering connection. Without that route the reply would have nowhere to go, so a one-way route is not enough. The security group is stateful, so the reply needs no extra inbound rule.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 886 0 R
/Prev 965 0 R
>>
endobj
967 0 obj
<<
/Title (requests arrive but replies cannot get back.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 812 0 R
/Prev 887 0 R
/Next 1015 0 R
>>
endobj
